      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. The key understandability issues are:\n1. Many unused imports (Connection, Jsoup, DataUtil, ParseTest, TestServer, etc.)\n2. Three unused helper methods (`trackSeen`, `isClosed`, `getReader`) that clutter the class but are never called by `canSelectWithHas()`\n3. The `basic()` method calls `parse()` twice on the same HTML — this is confusing but must be preserved to keep the same runtime behavior\n\nLet me write the improved test.Now I'll compile-check it.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused imports and three unused helper methods (`trackSeen`, `isClosed`, `getReader`), renames the vague variable `el` to `divWithParagraph`, and adds focused Javadoc comments explaining the `basic()` method's double-parse behavior and the intent of the `:has()` selector test — while keeping all method calls and assertions identical to the original."
